1
00:00:00,415 --> 00:00:02,970
This is Rahim, a hashish seller,

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:05,390
and the year is 1972.

3
00:00:05,864 --> 00:00:07,680
Kabul, Afghanistan.

4
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:09,940
His shutter jams halfway up.

5
00:00:10,302 --> 00:00:11,100
Блядь.

6
00:00:11,285 --> 00:00:13,190
He gives it another push.

7
00:00:14,608 --> 00:00:17,080
Outside, the bazaar is waking up.

8
00:00:17,410 --> 00:00:20,210
Bazaar comes from Persian: a market.

9
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:22,730
Bread, carpets, jewelry.

10
00:00:22,798 --> 00:00:25,590
The hippie trail brings foreign visitors.

11
00:00:25,844 --> 00:00:27,250
Another working morning.

12
00:00:28,655 --> 00:00:31,200
A traveler enters with a battered notebook.

13
00:00:31,346 --> 00:00:35,240
On one page: a cannabis leaf
and the word “indica.”

14
00:00:35,631 --> 00:00:36,890
Remember that word.

15
00:00:37,174 --> 00:00:39,830
Rahim puts two glasses on the counter.

16
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:42,770
Tea first.

17
00:00:43,126 --> 00:00:47,580
The visitor points at a small block
of cannabis resin, then at his money.

18
00:00:47,882 --> 00:00:50,410
Neither of them has agreed on a price yet.

19
00:00:50,681 --> 00:00:53,660
Enlightenment, apparently, requires a discount.

20
00:00:55,134 --> 00:00:57,960
His notebook says indica: “of India.”

21
00:00:58,579 --> 00:01:02,050
A botanical name, not proof
of where the plant grew.

22
00:01:02,456 --> 00:01:04,430
He has crossed half a continent.

23
00:01:04,703 --> 00:01:06,970
That word still isn’t a passport.

24
00:01:08,528 --> 00:01:12,330
Rahim watches a fresh tea ring
spread across the wood.

25
00:01:12,764 --> 00:01:14,190
Ёб твою мать.

26
00:01:14,505 --> 00:01:16,170
He reaches for a cloth.

27
00:01:16,379 --> 00:01:18,500
The traveler closes his notebook.

28
00:01:19,922 --> 00:01:22,140
By evening, the visitor is gone.

29
00:01:22,610 --> 00:01:25,850
Rahim puts away the scale
and pulls down the shutter.

30
00:01:26,369 --> 00:01:28,260
It catches in the same place.
